From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:35:34 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Review: the wall's cell size from true boundary edges;
 bands just past the floor are placed without slivers

- A ring's "wall edges" were any two consecutive wall vertices, so at a box
  corner a chord across the corner cell counted, and h came out up to about
  20% large. Only an edge of the domain boundary counts now.
- test_0904: a band 0.31 cells from the wall (h = 0.025) and 0.37 cells
  (h = 0.0125) is placed, the wall keeps its labels, and no cell anywhere
  is below half the deep placement's smallest angle (measured 22.5 and 24.3
  degrees against about 38). A threshold in mesh units, not cells, fails the
  finer case; an angle check below 0.6 cells was missing.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
